{
  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nThe nurse reviews a commercial driver's symptoms alongside information from a witness, the treating team and an older workplace form, because each source describes a different part of the story; the occupational record retains those differences and identifies completed current findings without turning a booking, a family account or a recollection into a measured patient result.\n\nThe driver explicitly denies any lifetime blackout, loss of consciousness or episode of impaired awareness, and the current nurse history confirms no blackout history; a sister's faint after standing in a hot room is recorded as family information, while the driver's own tiredness after an overnight route occurred with preserved awareness and no witness-reported unresponsiveness, rather than a confirmed episode being denied or reclassified after the fact.\n\nThe interview takes place before the driver's next planned roster, and the nurse records changes in symptoms, treatment and available documents without assuming that a future specialist appointment has already occurred; any letter that has been requested but not supplied remains separate from the findings actually available when this occupational record is written.\n\nThe nurse keeps the relevant current attachment with the record and identifies the older account by its timing, so a later reviewer can distinguish what was observed, what the driver reported and what remains unresolved; no additional measurement, specialist conclusion or diagnosis is added merely because it would make the occupational decision easier to complete.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
